  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is the exact plan for piped gas line provisioning?",
      "a": "The gas bank location and pipe routing are final. A private gas agency will supply every home through its own prepaid meter, managed like a mobile recharge, not by the Residents' Association."
    },
    {
      "q": "Will the clubhouse be fully functional in Phase 1?",
      "a": "Yes. The clubhouse will be completely built and fully functional as part of Phase 1 delivery."
    },
    {
      "q": "Are the primary power backup and water facilities shared with Phase 2?",
      "a": "No. Phase 1 has its own dedicated primary power backup (DG room/Transformer), Sewage Treatment Plant (STP), and underground water sump. Phase 2 will utilize its own separate infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "q": "How is day-to-day garbage disposal handled?",
      "a": "Waste is segregated and wet waste is processed entirely on-site via our own in-house Organic Waste Converter (OWC) located at the basement level."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the status of the adjacent garbage dump yard?",
      "a": "It is a private dump yard located entirely outside our boundary. It is situated approximately 230 meters from the site boundary and 280 meters from Wing F in a straight line."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do cabs and deliveries access the individual wings?",
      "a": "Cabs use one common pick-up point, and two buggies serve every wing to transport residents. However, deliveries go door-to-door directly to every wing."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the sustainable water plan for the eventual 1,250 flats?",
      "a": "There are currently 12 boreholes on site. We are actively using six of them for construction, and their yield is sufficient for all ongoing construction work."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is there provision for EV charging in visitor parking?",
      "a": "Yes. Phase 1 has four visitor-parking zones, and each zone gets an electrical provision for EV charging. The exact number of chargers will be decided by the Residents' Association."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who maintains Fire and BESCOM safety audits after handover?",
      "a": "At handover, fire and electrical approvals will be in place. Bricks & Milestones will maintain the building for the first year. After Year 1, the Residents' Association handles all renewals and inspections."
    }
  ],
